1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:07,841
♪ Oh, Mister Tailor… ♪
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

2
00:00:09,259 --> 00:00:13,138
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

3
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:17,767
Mercado on the phone: I know
you’re on leave.

4
00:00:17,851 --> 00:00:19,936
But I just had to let you know.

5
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:24,274
Samir escaped, just this morning
from the hospital.

6
00:00:24,357 --> 00:00:26,109
Be careful still.

7
00:00:26,192 --> 00:00:28,028
[panting]

8
00:00:28,528 --> 00:00:31,489
[gunshots]

9
00:00:31,573 --> 00:00:32,073
[music continues]

10
00:00:32,157 --> 00:00:33,408
[grunts]

11
00:00:33,491 --> 00:00:34,034
Who are you?

12
00:00:34,117 --> 00:00:35,076
Let’s move.

13
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:35,994
Uno: Before they catch up to us.

14
00:00:36,077 --> 00:00:38,121
What about the secret room?

15
00:00:38,204 --> 00:00:42,250
What secret room, love?

16
00:00:42,333 --> 00:00:46,421
Audrey: I thought the reason we moved
was to start again as a family?

17
00:00:46,921 --> 00:00:49,215
To leave your old life behind.

18
00:00:49,799 --> 00:00:51,384
But Atoy, you already have a family.

19
00:00:52,218 --> 00:00:53,970
Paldo: We don’t want anything bad to
happen to you, Atoy.

20
00:00:54,054 --> 00:00:54,721
We love you.

21
00:00:54,804 --> 00:00:56,431
All of these things here,

22
00:00:57,140 --> 00:00:58,975
they all came from the secret room.

23
00:00:59,059 --> 00:00:59,684
Audrey: Really?

24
00:00:59,768 --> 00:01:01,519
Ame: You’re retiring from being
a tracker, Atoy?

25
00:01:01,603 --> 00:01:03,897
But of course, I’m still a tailor by day,

26
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:06,691
but a father and husband for life.

27
00:01:06,775 --> 00:01:08,401
[chuckles]
That’s it!

28
00:01:08,985 --> 00:01:11,154
Gavin: Now I can be with you
anytime I want.

29
00:01:11,237 --> 00:01:13,323
Cita: Respect your Brother Atoy’s house.

30
00:01:13,406 --> 00:01:15,575
I won’t do anything you wouldn’t like.

31
00:01:15,658 --> 00:01:19,954
Have you told your boss that
you’re retiring?

32
00:01:20,038 --> 00:01:21,706
Children of the Thread…

33
00:01:21,790 --> 00:01:26,336
- Children of the Thread! Eyyy!
- Children of the Thread! Eyy! Ey!

34
00:01:26,419 --> 00:01:27,754
[laughs & applauds]
Wow.

35
00:01:27,837 --> 00:01:28,880
Hey, come on!
Come on, let’s go inside.

36
00:01:28,963 --> 00:01:30,590
Anthony Padua, is that you?

37
00:01:30,673 --> 00:01:31,341
Yes, Ma’am.

38
00:01:31,424 --> 00:01:32,300
That’s me.

39
00:01:32,801 --> 00:01:34,344
Oh my, Sir, it’s really you!

40
00:01:34,427 --> 00:01:36,805
I’m Jesabel Marie Garcia,

41
00:01:36,888 --> 00:01:39,057
executive secretary of Sir Mercado.

42
00:01:39,140 --> 00:01:40,809
Jesabel: I’m your new mission, Sir.

43
00:01:40,892 --> 00:01:43,520
I told you, I’ll just talk
to my boss. So…

44
00:01:43,603 --> 00:01:46,064
You’ll talk at Sir Mercado’s birthday
celebration instead.

45
00:01:46,147 --> 00:01:48,149
Atoy: He’s like a father
figure to me, right?

46
00:01:48,733 --> 00:01:50,860
I’ll tell him I’m retiring,

47
00:01:50,944 --> 00:01:52,904
that I’m leaving, you know.

48
00:01:52,987 --> 00:01:54,697
Artem: He leads an independent tracking

49
00:01:54,781 --> 00:01:57,909
and recovery organization
called The Agency.

50
00:01:58,576 --> 00:02:01,704
Then, we must be very careful.

51
00:02:02,789 --> 00:02:05,917
Gather all the information
and we will strike.

52
00:02:09,045 --> 00:02:10,088
[soft rock music playing]

53
00:02:10,171 --> 00:02:11,214
It’s so noisy.

54
00:02:11,297 --> 00:02:14,008
[motorcycle engine revving]

55
00:02:14,092 --> 00:02:16,970
[music continues]

56
00:02:18,346 --> 00:02:19,722
[music continues]

57
00:02:44,205 --> 00:02:45,874
Good evening, Mang Abe.

58
00:02:45,957 --> 00:02:47,584
Is he here?

59
00:02:48,334 --> 00:02:50,879
Sir Padua, The Master Cutter.

60
00:02:50,962 --> 00:02:52,005
Not yet.

61
00:02:52,088 --> 00:02:56,676
[music continues]

62
00:03:11,399 --> 00:03:12,150
[device blips]

63
00:03:13,526 --> 00:03:14,736
[music fades]

64
00:03:14,819 --> 00:03:17,155
Try the black frame.

65
00:03:19,032 --> 00:03:21,868
[soft rock music playing]

66
00:03:25,580 --> 00:03:26,831
[device blips]

67
00:03:29,083 --> 00:03:30,251
[door opens]

68
00:03:30,752 --> 00:03:33,171
[music continues]

69
00:03:45,308 --> 00:03:45,808
[music fades]

70
00:03:45,892 --> 00:03:49,395
[theme music playing]

71
00:03:49,479 --> 00:03:51,814
♪ Oh, Mister Tailor… ♪

72
00:03:51,898 --> 00:03:56,569
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

73
00:03:57,820 --> 00:04:00,031
♪ Wait a moment, Mister Tailor ♪

74
00:04:00,114 --> 00:04:01,366
♪ Can you be the one to sew ♪

75
00:04:01,449 --> 00:04:02,742
♪ The hole in my polo

76
00:04:02,825 --> 00:04:05,578
that fits just under the armpit ♪

77
00:04:05,662 --> 00:04:07,747
♪ In every cut of cloth ♪

78
00:04:07,830 --> 00:04:09,332
♪ There’s a secret behind it ♪

79
00:04:09,415 --> 00:04:11,251
♪ If your measurement is wrong ♪

80
00:04:11,334 --> 00:04:15,797
♪ The whole movement turns crooked… ♪

81
00:04:15,880 --> 00:04:16,506
[gunshots]

82
00:04:16,589 --> 00:04:18,258
♪ Oh, Mister Tailor ♪

83
00:04:18,341 --> 00:04:20,468
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

84
00:04:21,094 --> 00:04:22,220
[music swells]

85
00:04:27,308 --> 00:04:29,102
Jesabel: Your iced tea is too sweet.

86
00:04:29,185 --> 00:04:30,687
You should reduce the sugar a bit,

87
00:04:30,770 --> 00:04:33,523
our guests might get diabetes.

88
00:04:33,606 --> 00:04:37,360
And, that black coffee of Mercado's,

89
00:04:37,860 --> 00:04:40,613
it should be like water, but you
know, with a kick?

90
00:04:40,697 --> 00:04:41,948
That's how it should be.

91
00:04:42,031 --> 00:04:43,283
Oh, all right. You may go now.

92
00:04:43,366 --> 00:04:44,909
- Okay, Ma’am.
- The black coffee… don’t forget.

93
00:04:44,993 --> 00:04:46,411
I’ll make it now.

94
00:04:46,494 --> 00:04:47,161
Go.

95
00:04:48,538 --> 00:04:51,833
Jesabel, isn’t Sir Mercado here yet?

96
00:04:51,916 --> 00:04:54,961
Oh, he’s here, but he’s just backstage.

97
00:04:55,044 --> 00:04:57,171
He’s preparing his presentation for later.

98
00:04:58,673 --> 00:05:01,342
Are all the trackers here already?

99
00:05:01,426 --> 00:05:03,928
Ah, they should be complete.

100
00:05:04,012 --> 00:05:06,764
But Master Cutter isn’t here yet.

101
00:05:06,848 --> 00:05:08,141
Hopefully he arrives soon

102
00:05:08,224 --> 00:05:12,812
because Sir Mercado wants him to lead
the urgent mission.

103
00:05:13,813 --> 00:05:15,815
Mission? What mission?

104
00:05:16,649 --> 00:05:18,735
Uh, I don’t know the full details.

105
00:05:18,818 --> 00:05:23,698
But what I know is, they got
intel from Belladonna.

106
00:05:23,781 --> 00:05:29,370
And it’s connected to the international
terrorist group Obsidian.

107
00:05:29,454 --> 00:05:32,206
[suspicious music playing]

108
00:05:34,334 --> 00:05:37,211
Samir’s group? Did they return
to the Philippines?

109
00:05:37,295 --> 00:05:41,090
Uh-- I don’t know anything
about that.

110
00:05:41,966 --> 00:05:44,343
Only Sir Mercado knows everything.

111
00:05:47,847 --> 00:05:50,099
Bye. I still have something to attend to.

112
00:06:18,878 --> 00:06:20,630
[music fades]

113
00:06:24,801 --> 00:06:25,843
[thuds]

114
00:06:27,095 --> 00:06:28,137
[clatters]

115
00:06:37,188 --> 00:06:39,107
[thudding]

116
00:06:39,190 --> 00:06:42,777
[music continues]

117
00:06:48,825 --> 00:06:51,494
Do you have access to
the system now?

118
00:06:52,120 --> 00:06:55,081
[music continues]

119
00:06:56,082 --> 00:06:57,500
In five minutes.

120
00:06:57,583 --> 00:07:00,128
[music continues]

121
00:07:07,218 --> 00:07:09,137
[zipping]

122
00:07:09,220 --> 00:07:11,514
[music continues]

123
00:07:11,597 --> 00:07:12,473
[zips]

124
00:07:13,599 --> 00:07:16,227
[music continues]

125
00:07:30,867 --> 00:07:35,121
And a fine toast to
our new home,

126
00:07:35,621 --> 00:07:38,791
and to Barangay Tabang Lupa.

127
00:07:38,875 --> 00:07:39,417
[chuckles]

128
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:41,002
Janine: And let’s not forget.

129
00:07:41,085 --> 00:07:46,507
Also, a fine toast to our new
room and school.

130
00:07:46,591 --> 00:07:51,053
And most of all, to the
loves of my life.

131
00:07:51,637 --> 00:07:53,890
My beautiful family.

132
00:07:53,973 --> 00:07:57,643
Especially, my daughters.

133
00:07:57,727 --> 00:08:00,104
[elegant classical music playing]

134
00:08:00,188 --> 00:08:00,980
[gasps]

135
00:08:01,522 --> 00:08:03,399
I almost forgot!

136
00:08:04,901 --> 00:08:07,987
The toast to our father…

137
00:08:08,070 --> 00:08:09,697
Ohh…

138
00:08:09,780 --> 00:08:11,991
Daddy and Tatoy.

139
00:08:12,074 --> 00:08:13,284
Oh…

140
00:08:13,367 --> 00:08:16,162
And to his happy retirement!

141
00:08:16,245 --> 00:08:18,080
Yes, exactly.

142
00:08:18,164 --> 00:08:19,999
To his happy retirement!

143
00:08:20,082 --> 00:08:22,627
- [Ibyang] Yes.
- Retirement, indeed.

144
00:08:22,710 --> 00:08:23,252
[clinks]
[chuckles]

145
00:08:23,336 --> 00:08:26,464
- Let’s have tea.
- Oh, tea!

146
00:08:27,590 --> 00:08:30,885
[phone ringing]

147
00:08:30,968 --> 00:08:33,471
This iced tea… has a very nice taste.

148
00:08:33,554 --> 00:08:34,889
[muffled chattering in the distance]

149
00:08:34,972 --> 00:08:36,349
Oh, hello?

150
00:08:36,432 --> 00:08:38,476
Who am I speaking to?

151
00:08:39,143 --> 00:08:40,770
Sir, is that you?

152
00:08:41,771 --> 00:08:43,606
Uno on the phone:
This is Uno, Sir Atoy.

153
00:08:43,689 --> 00:08:44,857
[sneaky music playing]

154
00:08:44,941 --> 00:08:47,735
- Oh? Oh, Uno?
- Hmm. Amazing tea.

155
00:08:47,818 --> 00:08:49,987
- One of the best teas I’ve tried…
- How are you? Any news?

156
00:08:50,071 --> 00:08:51,531
Janine: … in my whole entire life.

157
00:08:51,614 --> 00:08:52,907
Sorry, I couldn’t--

158
00:08:52,990 --> 00:08:54,408
I was playing with my kids.

159
00:08:54,492 --> 00:08:55,576
Uhm, how are you there?

160
00:08:56,577 --> 00:08:57,870
They’re looking for you, Sir.

161
00:08:58,538 --> 00:09:01,415
Looks like this won’t start until
attendance is complete.

162
00:09:01,499 --> 00:09:03,709
[music continues]

163
00:09:03,793 --> 00:09:04,460
You know, Sir,

164
00:09:05,294 --> 00:09:08,256
I really don’t feel good
about this event.

165
00:09:09,882 --> 00:09:11,175
[music continues]

166
00:09:11,259 --> 00:09:12,343
But I don’t know why.

167
00:09:13,386 --> 00:09:14,512
I can’t figure it out.

168
00:09:14,595 --> 00:09:15,888
Atoy on the phone: Relax.

169
00:09:15,972 --> 00:09:17,390
Just talk to them.

170
00:09:18,015 --> 00:09:19,684
Anyway. I’m on my way.

171
00:09:19,767 --> 00:09:20,810
I’ll get ready.

172
00:09:21,727 --> 00:09:24,981
Just encode my profile number,
while I’m not there, okay?

173
00:09:25,064 --> 00:09:27,525
So you can start already,
so it’s complete.

174
00:09:28,359 --> 00:09:30,152
Atoy on the phone:
Sir Abe knows me.

175
00:09:30,236 --> 00:09:31,362
He can take care of it.

176
00:09:31,445 --> 00:09:32,363
Copy, Sir.

177
00:09:32,446 --> 00:09:33,072
Atoy on the phone: All right.

178
00:09:49,255 --> 00:09:52,091
[music swells]

179
00:09:52,174 --> 00:09:55,386
[suspicious music playing]

180
00:09:59,056 --> 00:10:01,434
Ladies, can I have one?

181
00:10:01,517 --> 00:10:02,893
Ah, of course.

182
00:10:02,977 --> 00:10:04,103
Of course.

183
00:10:04,186 --> 00:10:05,563
Ta-ta!

184
00:10:05,646 --> 00:10:06,272
Bye, bye.

185
00:10:09,692 --> 00:10:11,944
[rousing music playing]

186
00:10:12,862 --> 00:10:14,739
[muffled chattering in the distance]

187
00:10:14,822 --> 00:10:15,323
[Staff] Wait.

188
00:10:15,823 --> 00:10:17,533
Is that Sir Mercado’s iced coffee?

189
00:10:18,492 --> 00:10:20,286
Bring it backstage,
he’s there.

190
00:10:21,037 --> 00:10:21,996
No sugar, okay.

191
00:10:22,747 --> 00:10:24,999
Waiter: Oh, I put a little syrup.

192
00:10:25,499 --> 00:10:26,125
Oh no.

193
00:10:26,959 --> 00:10:27,585
Do it again.

194
00:10:27,668 --> 00:10:29,462
Ma’am Jesabel will scold us.

195
00:10:29,545 --> 00:10:31,922
[music continues]

196
00:10:40,014 --> 00:10:42,516
Samir, the trackers are complete.

197
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:44,560
[music continues]

198
00:10:44,644 --> 00:10:45,144
Are you sure?

199
00:10:45,227 --> 00:10:46,979
I don’t see him anywhere.

200
00:10:48,898 --> 00:10:50,358
[laptop blipping]

201
00:10:50,441 --> 00:10:51,901
Artem: He is the last
one to encode.

202
00:10:52,652 --> 00:10:53,903
He has arrived and…

203
00:10:54,737 --> 00:10:56,030
he might be around.

204
00:10:56,113 --> 00:10:57,990
Tell everyone to get ready.

205
00:10:58,616 --> 00:10:59,825
No one leaves here.

206
00:11:00,409 --> 00:11:00,993
Copy.

207
00:11:01,077 --> 00:11:03,579
[music continues]

208
00:11:04,121 --> 00:11:05,706
No. I think he is backstage.

209
00:11:05,790 --> 00:11:07,083
I will proceed.

210
00:11:07,166 --> 00:11:10,419
Artem: Everybody, prepare
for phase two.

211
00:11:11,295 --> 00:11:12,171
Let’s go!

212
00:11:14,799 --> 00:11:16,008
[car doors close]

213
00:11:22,223 --> 00:11:24,975
[rousing music playing]

214
00:11:26,936 --> 00:11:30,064
[tense music playing]

215
00:11:43,369 --> 00:11:45,704
[car engine stops]

216
00:11:45,788 --> 00:11:50,292
[mysterious music playing]

217
00:11:51,919 --> 00:11:53,754
[music swells]

218
00:12:12,440 --> 00:12:17,862
[car engine revving]

219
00:12:18,571 --> 00:12:20,156
[music fades]

220
00:12:20,239 --> 00:12:20,865
[bullets whizzing]

221
00:12:20,948 --> 00:12:21,615
[tense music playing]

222
00:12:21,699 --> 00:12:22,825
Artem: Get this man
out of here!

223
00:12:26,328 --> 00:12:28,330
[music continues]

224
00:12:30,332 --> 00:12:32,251
Now, pull down the shutters.

225
00:12:32,334 --> 00:12:35,045
[clanging]

226
00:12:35,129 --> 00:12:38,966
[keys jingling]

227
00:12:40,259 --> 00:12:42,928
[music swells]

228
00:12:43,012 --> 00:12:44,847
[crickets chirping in the distance]

229
00:12:46,557 --> 00:12:52,771
[footsteps tapping]

230
00:12:52,855 --> 00:12:56,734
[suspicious music playing]

231
00:13:19,673 --> 00:13:25,846
[upbeat music playing]

232
00:13:50,913 --> 00:13:54,083
[tense music playing]

233
00:13:54,875 --> 00:13:55,834
Relax.

234
00:13:57,002 --> 00:14:00,506
Uno Alcaraz, a.k.a
The Firefighter.

235
00:14:01,090 --> 00:14:02,299
Long time no see.

236
00:14:03,008 --> 00:14:05,344
The Baker.
How are you?

237
00:14:06,011 --> 00:14:07,304
When was…

238
00:14:07,930 --> 00:14:09,223
our last mission?

239
00:14:09,848 --> 00:14:12,643
Two years ago. The missing pastor.

240
00:14:12,726 --> 00:14:14,395
Oh, I see.

241
00:14:14,478 --> 00:14:15,938
[suspicious music playing]

242
00:14:16,021 --> 00:14:18,107
[smirks] Yes, that was a long time ago.

243
00:14:18,190 --> 00:14:21,026
Wait. You must be The Firefighter.

244
00:14:21,527 --> 00:14:25,698
Congrats on tracking
the most wanted bagman, Rizaldo Coloma.

245
00:14:25,781 --> 00:14:27,658
Everybody thought he was
hiding in Europe.

246
00:14:27,741 --> 00:14:29,535
Turns out he was just
in Velora Bay.

247
00:14:29,618 --> 00:14:33,247
Actually, Rizaldo Coloma wasn’t
really my job order.

248
00:14:33,914 --> 00:14:36,166
He was assigned to
The Master Cutter.

249
00:14:37,334 --> 00:14:40,045
Oh, so, where’s the
legendary Master Cutter?

250
00:14:40,671 --> 00:14:41,714
Is he here already?

251
00:14:42,464 --> 00:14:43,716
Baker: We were together
in a mission,

252
00:14:43,799 --> 00:14:44,925
I think…

253
00:14:45,009 --> 00:14:46,302
three or four years ago.

254
00:14:47,303 --> 00:14:49,263
I would love to meet him.

255
00:14:49,346 --> 00:14:51,473
[music continues]

256
00:14:52,099 --> 00:14:53,100
He’s late.

257
00:15:58,248 --> 00:15:59,333
Good evening!

258
00:15:59,875 --> 00:16:02,670
I hope you’re enjoying meeting
everyone here!

259
00:16:02,753 --> 00:16:04,797
Host: But I think, now
it’s time to meet

260
00:16:04,880 --> 00:16:08,092
the man of the hour,
our birthday boy…

261
00:16:08,175 --> 00:16:12,096
[foreboding music playing]

262
00:16:12,179 --> 00:16:14,390
The Agency’s backbone!

263
00:16:15,182 --> 00:16:16,725
Our beloved,

264
00:16:16,809 --> 00:16:20,020
Retired Colonel
Levi Mercado!

265
00:16:20,521 --> 00:16:27,486
[applauding]

266
00:16:31,448 --> 00:16:33,242
[music continues]

267
00:16:33,325 --> 00:16:36,328
Uhm, Mr. Mercado.

268
00:16:36,412 --> 00:16:37,663
Don’t be shy, Sir.

269
00:16:42,209 --> 00:16:43,669
[music swells]

270
00:16:45,838 --> 00:16:52,803
[intense music playing]

271
00:17:04,648 --> 00:17:08,027
[footsteps tapping]

272
00:17:16,869 --> 00:17:22,249
[suspicious music playing]

273
00:17:29,298 --> 00:17:30,632
Atoy: Sir Abe?

274
00:17:31,258 --> 00:17:35,471
[music continues]

275
00:17:35,846 --> 00:17:37,723
Sir Abe.

276
00:17:38,348 --> 00:17:41,810
[music continues]

277
00:17:56,408 --> 00:17:58,160
[music fades]

278
00:18:05,626 --> 00:18:09,963
[ominous music playing]

279
00:18:20,641 --> 00:18:27,564
[tranquilizer darts whizzing]

280
00:18:31,860 --> 00:18:34,279
[screaming & panicking]

281
00:18:35,280 --> 00:18:36,073
[ominous music playing]

282
00:18:37,658 --> 00:18:40,410
[screaming & panicking]

283
00:18:41,995 --> 00:18:44,164
[darts & bullets whizzing]

284
00:18:44,248 --> 00:18:45,582
[music fades]

285
00:18:49,169 --> 00:18:50,337
Bro.

286
00:18:50,420 --> 00:18:51,296
- Hey.
- Do you still have cigarettes?

287
00:18:52,297 --> 00:18:54,133
Goon 2: No, there’s none left.
So, let’s go?

288
00:18:54,216 --> 00:18:57,177
[music continues]

289
00:19:00,264 --> 00:19:03,016
[tense music playing]

290
00:19:03,559 --> 00:19:04,101
Goon 2: Let’s go.

291
00:19:04,184 --> 00:19:05,227
Goon 1: Wait.

292
00:19:05,310 --> 00:19:07,271
Let’s wait for Sir Samir’s
signal first.

293
00:19:07,354 --> 00:19:08,021
[music continues]

294
00:19:08,105 --> 00:19:15,028
[darts whizzing & gunshots]

295
00:19:16,238 --> 00:19:19,658
[thuds, then clatters]

296
00:19:19,741 --> 00:19:20,993
[gunshots & darts whizzing]

297
00:19:21,076 --> 00:19:21,952
[groans]

298
00:19:22,452 --> 00:19:23,787
Idiots!

299
00:19:23,871 --> 00:19:25,706
You are not supposed to kill
the trackers!

300
00:19:25,789 --> 00:19:26,331
Move!

301
00:19:26,415 --> 00:19:28,667
[music continues]

302
00:19:36,425 --> 00:19:38,385
[music fades]

303
00:19:38,468 --> 00:19:40,095
[crickets chirping in distance]

304
00:19:40,179 --> 00:19:44,183
[rock music playing]

305
00:19:46,810 --> 00:19:47,519
[grunts and groans]

306
00:19:47,603 --> 00:19:48,145
[dagger swishes]

307
00:19:48,228 --> 00:19:51,857
[groaning]

308
00:19:51,940 --> 00:19:52,858
[dagger swishing & thumping]

309
00:19:52,941 --> 00:19:54,359
[groans]

310
00:19:54,526 --> 00:19:58,155
[dagger swishing & thumping]

311
00:19:58,238 --> 00:20:04,745
[grunting, groaning, growling]

312
00:20:05,329 --> 00:20:06,663
[thuds]

313
00:20:13,295 --> 00:20:14,254
[thuds]

314
00:20:16,548 --> 00:20:19,843
[groans]

315
00:20:19,927 --> 00:20:21,887
[music continues]

316
00:20:21,970 --> 00:20:24,640
[footsteps tapping]

317
00:20:24,723 --> 00:20:27,392
[tense music playing]

318
00:20:35,108 --> 00:20:36,568
I know Samir is
behind this.

319
00:20:36,652 --> 00:20:40,697
[music continues]

320
00:20:40,781 --> 00:20:41,531
Gotcha.

321
00:20:49,790 --> 00:20:51,708
Atoy: Son of a thread.

322
00:20:51,792 --> 00:20:55,337
[music continues]

323
00:20:58,048 --> 00:21:03,637
[phone ringing]

324
00:21:03,720 --> 00:21:04,680
[phone blips]

325
00:21:04,763 --> 00:21:06,390
Foreign man on the phone:
Evacuate your positions.

326
00:21:06,473 --> 00:21:08,225
The bombs are in place.

327
00:21:08,308 --> 00:21:10,769
Samir and Artem are
already secured.

328
00:21:10,852 --> 00:21:11,561
[phone blips]

329
00:21:11,645 --> 00:21:13,563
[tense music playing]

330
00:21:13,647 --> 00:21:15,440
[rope squeaks]

331
00:21:17,025 --> 00:21:19,987
[suspicious music playing]

332
00:21:22,447 --> 00:21:23,365
Hurry up, men!

333
00:21:26,702 --> 00:21:28,412
[music swells]

334
00:21:32,291 --> 00:21:34,293
[suspenseful music playing]

335
00:21:34,376 --> 00:21:38,046
[explosion]

336
00:21:38,130 --> 00:21:39,881
[music continues]

337
00:21:59,776 --> 00:22:00,819
[music fades]

338
00:22:00,902 --> 00:22:03,864
[footsteps tapping]

339
00:22:05,198 --> 00:22:07,409
[pensive music playing]

340
00:22:07,492 --> 00:22:08,744
Do you have Mercado?

341
00:22:08,827 --> 00:22:10,245
We’ve removed the
body already.

342
00:22:10,329 --> 00:22:11,580
Where is Atoy?

343
00:22:12,622 --> 00:22:13,790
Could’ve been
taken out.

344
00:22:14,583 --> 00:22:15,417
So, we must leave!

345
00:22:17,336 --> 00:22:18,879
[music continues]

346
00:22:24,509 --> 00:22:25,761
Proceed with phase three.

347
00:22:27,471 --> 00:22:30,307
[music swells]

348
00:22:32,893 --> 00:22:35,437
[tense music playing]

349
00:22:35,520 --> 00:22:37,189
[music fades]

350
00:22:37,272 --> 00:22:38,398
[clanging]

351
00:22:39,274 --> 00:22:39,816
Tikboy: Brother, Brother!

352
00:22:40,400 --> 00:22:41,359
[gunshot]

353
00:22:41,443 --> 00:22:42,360
What's going on inside?!

354
00:22:42,903 --> 00:22:44,404
There's been gunfire for
a while!

355
00:22:44,488 --> 00:22:45,822
Something even exploded!

356
00:22:46,865 --> 00:22:48,116
Brother.

357
00:22:48,200 --> 00:22:50,535
[music continues]

358
00:22:50,619 --> 00:22:52,412
Of all times, I don’t have my
ring right now.

359
00:22:52,496 --> 00:22:54,498
[clanging]

360
00:22:54,581 --> 00:22:55,665
Open the other side.

361
00:22:56,917 --> 00:22:57,876
[music continues]

362
00:22:58,710 --> 00:22:59,795
Is it okay now?

363
00:22:59,878 --> 00:23:00,629
Come on, help me.

364
00:23:01,671 --> 00:23:05,050
[metal clanging & screeching]

365
00:23:06,510 --> 00:23:07,594
Sir Abe?

366
00:23:09,054 --> 00:23:09,721
Come on.

367
00:23:09,805 --> 00:23:11,223
Atoy: Sir Abe?

368
00:23:12,099 --> 00:23:13,266
[music fades]

369
00:23:13,350 --> 00:23:15,644
[tense music playing]

370
00:23:45,799 --> 00:23:47,217
[music fades]

371
00:23:51,012 --> 00:23:54,474
[pensive music playing]

372
00:24:16,329 --> 00:24:20,083
Atoy: Uno? Uno!

373
00:24:23,378 --> 00:24:24,296
Uno.

374
00:24:24,379 --> 00:24:26,423
What happened here?

375
00:24:27,090 --> 00:24:28,967
Backstage…

376
00:24:29,593 --> 00:24:31,344
Sir Mercado--

377
00:24:31,428 --> 00:24:32,304
Backstage?

378
00:24:35,390 --> 00:24:36,308
I’ll come back for you.

379
00:24:36,391 --> 00:24:41,396
[music continues]

380
00:25:15,513 --> 00:25:16,014
[music fades]

381
00:25:25,357 --> 00:25:28,360
Belladonna.
[mouthing words]

382
00:25:32,906 --> 00:25:34,282
[music swells]

383
00:25:34,366 --> 00:25:39,829
[electronic blipping]

384
00:25:39,913 --> 00:25:44,459
[intense music playing]

385
00:25:44,542 --> 00:25:46,169
OMG, Brother! Was there
an explosion?

386
00:25:46,253 --> 00:25:48,505
It says here it was
a terrorist attack.

387
00:25:48,588 --> 00:25:51,591
Samir’s group attacked the
event last night.

388
00:25:51,675 --> 00:25:53,176
Your mortal enemy has returned.

389
00:25:53,260 --> 00:25:55,845
More than twenty bodies
are missing.

390
00:25:55,929 --> 00:25:58,265
They all had different jobs
and backgrounds.

391
00:25:58,348 --> 00:26:00,642
Remi De Dios, a baker
in Bulacan.

392
00:26:01,142 --> 00:26:03,937
Lobert Villa, a barber
in Laguna.

393
00:26:04,020 --> 00:26:06,898
Ronalyn Tapales, a saleslady in Cebu.

394
00:26:07,440 --> 00:26:08,775
The common denominator:

395
00:26:08,858 --> 00:26:10,777
they all had military
backgrounds.

396
00:26:10,860 --> 00:26:12,862
I want to help
you with your…

397
00:26:12,946 --> 00:26:13,571
secret mission.

398
00:26:13,655 --> 00:26:15,532
Have you thought of a
way to find Samir?

399
00:26:15,615 --> 00:26:16,825
Please help me.

400
00:26:16,908 --> 00:26:17,993
Oh, here she is.

401
00:26:18,076 --> 00:26:19,577
Antonia! Come here.

402
00:26:19,661 --> 00:26:20,287
[giggles]

403
00:26:20,370 --> 00:26:22,038
Here’s Antonia.

404
00:26:23,832 --> 00:26:24,958
Excuse me.

405
00:26:26,042 --> 00:26:27,877
Samir: I am Frank Cohen.

406
00:26:27,961 --> 00:26:30,588
I’m here to meet
Danny Guo.

407
00:26:30,672 --> 00:26:31,673
♪ Like a bubble, like a bubble ♪

408
00:26:31,756 --> 00:26:32,340
♪ When the one who cuts ♪

409
00:26:32,424 --> 00:26:33,550
♪ knows how to do it right ♪

410
00:26:33,633 --> 00:26:36,594
[music continues]
